[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-122440"] :question/problem "Which of the following gives the line integral of the function $f(x,y)=x{e}^{y}$ along the quarter-circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=16,$ traversed from the point $(0,-4)$ to the point $(4,0)$ in the fourth quadrant?" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe curve $C$ is a part-circle of radius $4$ centered at $O,$ shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066920/assets/0baaafbe9846ccef2c06a3b1a86eccac394344afc2dfd94bba2907ebb1cf2362.png)\n\nThe curve $C$ can be parametrized as \n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,\\frac{3\\pi }{2}\\le t\\le 2\\pi .\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{sin}^{2}⁡t+16{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=x{e}^{y},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{e}^{4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}x{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{e}^{4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\cdot 4\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =16{\\int }_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{e}^{4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-122576/selection/109a3513d7c11252ff73fb07325ff9dfb90b0c9e16123f018fd88bb0b25e60c4" :answer/id #uuid "6b540412-fb2a-5b6a-b348-c7da441e4824" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\sqrt[3]{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122576/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "ef53b03d-aeed-571f-be0a-8c3ae73d4c2e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122576/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "1b340d24-d37d-51e7-9982-4014c14fff51" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122576/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "5f974ac2-483f-5772-b9f5-eaf5c71f278e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122576/selection/4d31c9cc5368f8cb8fa2d5661886836ed8f2cebf6125f1b80fa1f903bde9bebe" :answer/id #uuid "ee828b3e-e473-596e-85f7-3e0fd1af502e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122576/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "651a1703-0c2f-55f2-8943-f99e23f62f98" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-122576/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-122576/selection/109a3513d7c11252ff73fb07325ff9dfb90b0c9e16123f018fd88bb0b25e60c4" "q-122576/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-122576/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-122576/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-122576/selection/4d31c9cc5368f8cb8fa2d5661886836ed8f2cebf6125f1b80fa1f903bde9bebe"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122576" :question/id #uuid "f7752cbf-08cf-5d87-a957-774e73db29fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-122576" :question/problem "Evaluate the line integral of the function $f(x,y)=x\\sqrt[3]{y+1}$ along the circle $C$ with equation ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=36.$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe curve $C$ is a circle of radius $6$ centered at $O.$ It can be parametrized as \n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,0\\le t\\le 2\\pi .\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36{sin}^{2}⁡t+36{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=x\\sqrt[3]{y+1},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\sqrt[3]{6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\sqrt[3]{6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+1}\\cdot 6\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =6{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\sqrt[3]{6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+1}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this using the substitution $u=6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+1,$ $\\text{d}u=6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\sqrt[3]{6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+1}\\,\\text{d}t & =6{\\int }_{1}^{1}\\sqrt[3]{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =6(0) \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-122576/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3c33b34e-5b57-51c1-91d0-e098364bcdfb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122576"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-122586/selection/1403438fa710f6dd0316a6e2e2f5cd1905ca2621f150e23b5d70be89274f4118" :answer/id #uuid "6720c71e-bf94-5157-992a-646387a565be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}{cos}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122586/selection/803eb6b084ed2fc7a01643e8e6f2e2ba991784384d96f5be12c78b88747471fa" :answer/id #uuid "a9b7927a-d025-5449-bb92-0d1ae5714112" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122586/selection/e263d8981dd1c71b8a26fd26dc412d0b6dbcff785dff17eeb85414393636220c" :answer/id #uuid "f8df536b-9828-55d1-a5d8-b2c815d0ff45" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122586/selection/8ecadb3d491f93a2c1db4713e15934509f59e12ce782ffac352d6e62a3aa9444" :answer/id #uuid "46afe35a-b76a-598a-a8a2-29051f66cb84" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }{cos}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122586/selection/8e05ed29ec53d4b826faccc1f96248c5501400fde67f5ba293078ade9fb9c73c" :answer/id #uuid "ebae7482-f777-5b07-8446-e419b7aecf9a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8{\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}{sin}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122586/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ed03dcbc-c76f-58e5-8b96-ed8d21754b75" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-122586/selection/e263d8981dd1c71b8a26fd26dc412d0b6dbcff785dff17eeb85414393636220c" :answer-field/choices ["q-122586/selection/1403438fa710f6dd0316a6e2e2f5cd1905ca2621f150e23b5d70be89274f4118" "q-122586/selection/803eb6b084ed2fc7a01643e8e6f2e2ba991784384d96f5be12c78b88747471fa" "q-122586/selection/e263d8981dd1c71b8a26fd26dc412d0b6dbcff785dff17eeb85414393636220c" "q-122586/selection/8ecadb3d491f93a2c1db4713e15934509f59e12ce782ffac352d6e62a3aa9444" "q-122586/selection/8e05ed29ec53d4b826faccc1f96248c5501400fde67f5ba293078ade9fb9c73c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122586" :question/id #uuid "7aa8bcd7-fed3-5186-b1c1-b187da2c7965" :question/math-academy-id "q-122586" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the line integral of the function $f(x,y)=y\\,\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}$ along the quarter-circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4,$ traversed from the point $(0,2)$ to the point $(-2,0)$ in the second quadrant?" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe curve $C$ is a part-circle of radius $2$ centered at $O,$ shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066920/assets/d0ae53dd5d0932cbf834a166e851c227f75cb546b591a9fd43930ec06f0e9ddf.png)\n\nThe curve $C$ can be parametrized as \n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le t\\le \\pi .\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{sin}^{2}⁡t+4{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=y\\,\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\sqrt{4-(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\sqrt{4-4{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\sqrt{4{sin}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =4{sin}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}y\\,\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }4{sin}^{2}⁡t\\cdot 2\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =8{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-122586/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb008515-d668-509b-8c8a-76e892e709cc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122586"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-122591/selection/4f07480a4c15cd73cd348faf8fc2319be844c539fe48d5e27bf88827f846e513" :answer/id #uuid "815a9ce4-8a9e-52df-9203-3c47063c150f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16{\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}{sin}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122591/selection/8e05ed29ec53d4b826faccc1f96248c5501400fde67f5ba293078ade9fb9c73c" :answer/id #uuid "2bcd5417-c265-5c0e-940e-e49d451bafbb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8{\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}{sin}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122591/selection/e5c96e0ecf15a1ffe3b27e5848abd95a92f376ad3156ee88fc3784e81fa44c48" :answer/id #uuid "883b6f90-4e44-5d00-928e-f2a8afcabe13" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16{\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}{cos}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122591/selection/57234579ec2195c2499d5f0f413deafca61c549969ca313069ef04bb9183f6da" :answer/id #uuid "fc45b25a-96e6-5c4f-882b-de3fbeefa221" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8{\\int }_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }{cos}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122591/selection/805b735dc473bedd56505c2d73c6d577d1feac2beb28c2cc7c892831f344135b" :answer/id #uuid "203663f0-e4fa-5bee-a49a-710dab722a70" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16{\\int }_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }{cos}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122591/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3f222c2d-1d67-5b8b-8f80-a3ef50cb0148" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-122591/selection/e5c96e0ecf15a1ffe3b27e5848abd95a92f376ad3156ee88fc3784e81fa44c48" :answer-field/choices ["q-122591/selection/4f07480a4c15cd73cd348faf8fc2319be844c539fe48d5e27bf88827f846e513" "q-122591/selection/8e05ed29ec53d4b826faccc1f96248c5501400fde67f5ba293078ade9fb9c73c" "q-122591/selection/e5c96e0ecf15a1ffe3b27e5848abd95a92f376ad3156ee88fc3784e81fa44c48" "q-122591/selection/57234579ec2195c2499d5f0f413deafca61c549969ca313069ef04bb9183f6da" "q-122591/selection/805b735dc473bedd56505c2d73c6d577d1feac2beb28c2cc7c892831f344135b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122591" :question/id #uuid "7a882cfb-b3f3-519e-9b6e-6e0eebe95df2" :question/math-academy-id "q-122591" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the line integral of the function $f(x,y)=2{x}^{2}$ along the quarter-circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4,$ traversed from the point $(-2,0)$ to the point $(0,-2)$ in the third quadrant?" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe curve $C$ is a part-circle of radius $2$ centered at $O,$ shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066920/assets/1fd6c2df8b8467a46ed36b515842b88656883733376ee732839bab4085ca019c.png)\n\nThe curve $C$ can be parametrized as \n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,\\pi \\le t\\le \\frac{3\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{sin}^{2}⁡t+4{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=2{x}^{2},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =2(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2} \\\\  & =8{cos}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}2{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}8{cos}^{2}⁡t\\cdot 2\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =16{\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}{cos}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-122591/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb008515-d668-509b-8c8a-76e892e709cc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122591"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-122594/selection/01bbf8ebd5069470431f8452e98a426e151975cb8793ee4f306144a87060a9a3" :answer/id #uuid "84e27d12-f336-52f9-baff-901d2d2eeae9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122594/selection/77e5f609e5d8d491060e3a10614d0baf017b9dbf04da6561c7e9cb8462621053" :answer/id #uuid "a5e14576-b4c1-58c9-96bb-49e903faea0b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-18\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122594/selection/a996cecead059c2e05b8ded2ceb60e4e2170a4344e0c20625524ed13b23c6fbe" :answer/id #uuid "fe161fc8-cc44-59ef-80d4-36624be86331" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122594/selection/3320f524410fe76d49a95a9788fe8a6345a62ea05fb59862ddb7f2ecef5b6261" :answer/id #uuid "af6af82e-9fda-5e70-9681-c906c95b7d2e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{9\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122594/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "e42e4650-7663-5d04-aa21-52c2c1478455" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122594/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "83ec200b-d80e-59da-8330-6e370e4d9b76" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-122594/selection/77e5f609e5d8d491060e3a10614d0baf017b9dbf04da6561c7e9cb8462621053" :answer-field/choices ["q-122594/selection/01bbf8ebd5069470431f8452e98a426e151975cb8793ee4f306144a87060a9a3" "q-122594/selection/77e5f609e5d8d491060e3a10614d0baf017b9dbf04da6561c7e9cb8462621053" "q-122594/selection/a996cecead059c2e05b8ded2ceb60e4e2170a4344e0c20625524ed13b23c6fbe" "q-122594/selection/3320f524410fe76d49a95a9788fe8a6345a62ea05fb59862ddb7f2ecef5b6261" "q-122594/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122594" :question/id #uuid "2c494e76-b8ff-570a-84f4-aa9af6bfbb6e" :question/math-academy-id "q-122594" :question/problem "Evaluate the line integral of the function $f(x,y)=2x-3$ along the circle $C$ with equation ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=9.$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe curve $C$ is a circle of radius $3$ centered at $O.$ It can be parametrized as \n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,0\\le t\\le 2\\pi .\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9{sin}^{2}⁡t+9{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=2x-3,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =2(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)-3 \\\\  & =3(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }3(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-1)\\cdot 3\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =9{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-1)\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-1)\\,\\text{d}t & =9[2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-t]_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =9[2(0-0)-(2\\pi -0)] \\\\  & =-18\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-122594/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3c33b34e-5b57-51c1-91d0-e098364bcdfb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122594"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
